<IntegrationLayout title="Integration terms of use" description="Terms for using the private account connections operated by Maxfield Allison.">
<p>Effective September 10, 2026. These terms apply to the private applications listed under <a href="/integrations">Integrations</a>, operated by Maxfield Allison. Read the relevant application page and <a href="/integrations/privacy">privacy policy</a> before authorizing a connection.</p>
<h2>Who can use them</h2>
<p>Access is arranged directly with Maxfield. Connect only accounts you control or are authorized to connect, and include shared data only when you have permission to copy it into the destination service. Access to an account does not override an organization's rules or another person's sharing restrictions.</p>
<h2>What authorization allows</h2>
<p>You authorize the actions described on the application's page within the permissions you grant. For writable calendar synchronization, that includes copying event changes and deletions between connected services. Keep your accounts and devices secure, and report unexpected access or changes.</p>
<p>For Haliphron Backups, authorization covers uploading, reading and maintaining the application's encrypted Drive repository, including retention changes agreed for it. Backups use your available storage. Protect the encryption password and keep independent copies: successful upload alone does not establish that an application can be restored, and encryption does not prevent repository deletion or account loss.</p>
<p>For Haliphron Google Read, authorization covers retrieving information for the requested work and processing it through the selected AI service as described on the application page. AI results may be inaccurate or incomplete. Verify consequential information in the original service. Read access does not authorize Google account changes.</p>
<p>Haliphron Google Actions is not yet available. Any future workflow needs its own described scope and execution authority before use. Account consent does not itself approve every message, file change or other action that a credential could perform.</p>
<h2>Availability and changes</h2>
<p>These are personal services with no guaranteed availability, update interval, or support response time. Connections can fail or be paused for maintenance. Check important information in the source service and keep a separate backup where losing it would matter.</p>
<p>An integration may change or be discontinued. Changes to account access or data use will be described before renewed consent is requested. Existing authorization is not permission for an unrelated feature.</p>
<h2>Stopping a connection</h2>
<p>You can revoke provider access or ask Maxfield to stop the connection. Revocation and deletion are separate: the <a href="/integrations/privacy">privacy policy</a> explains retained copies and deletion requests. A connection may also be suspended to address a fault, unauthorized access, or misuse.</p>
<p>Google, Nextcloud hosting, and other connected services may have their own terms. This application is independently operated and is not endorsed by Google.</p>
<p>For questions or support, email <a href="mailto:maxfield.allison@gmail.com" data-umami-event="email-click">maxfield.allison@gmail.com</a>.</p>
</IntegrationLayout>
